<body>
    <h1>AI-354 - AI+ Configuration and Security</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p></p>
<p>This guide provides a comprehensive overview of setting up HashiCorp Vau=
lt and Consul for AI+, with a focus on deployment in containerized environm=
ents. It covers both standalone and clustered deployments, and consideratio=
ns for future Kubernetes integration. While this guide focuses on container=
ized deployments, the principles apply to non-containerized environments as=
 well.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Important</strong>: This guide assumes that TLS is used for all =
communication between Vault and Consul, even in non-clustered, air-gapped e=
nvironments. Mutual TLS (mTLS) will be used where applicable.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-Vault">Vault</h3>
<p>Vault is a tool for securely managing secrets. It provides a unified int=
erface to any secret, tight access control, and record logging. In this set=
up, we'll use Consul as the storage backend for Vault.</p>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-Consul">Consul</h3>
<p>Consul is a service mesh solution providing a full-featured control plan=
e with service discovery, configuration, and orchestration capabilities. In=
 this guide, Consul is used as a highly available, distributed key-value st=
ore for Vault.</p>
<h2 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-CertificateGeneration">Certifi=
cate Generation</h2>
<p>For TLS encryption, you'll need to generate:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>A Certificate Authority (CA) certificate</p></li>
<li>
<p>Server certificates for Vault and Consul</p></li>
<li>
<p>Client certificates for mTLS authentication</p></li>
</ol>
<p>Here's a brief example using OpenSSL:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence"># Creat=
e a CA
openssl genrsa -out ca.key 4096
openssl req -new -x509 -key ca.key -sha256 -subj "/CN=3Dvault-ca" -out ca.c=
rt

# Create certificates for Consul
openssl genrsa -out consul.key 2048
openssl req -new -key consul.key -out consul.csr -subj "/CN=3Dconsul"
openssl x509 -req -in consul.csr -CA ca.crt -CAkey ca.key -CAcreateserial -=
out consul.crt

# Create certificates for Vault
openssl genrsa -out vault.key 2048
openssl req -new -key vault.key -out vault.csr -subj "/CN=3Dvault"
openssl x509 -req -in vault.csr -CA ca.crt -CAkey ca.key -CAcreateserial -o=
ut vault.crt
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-VaultSetup">Vault Setup</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-Pre-Conditions">Pre-Conditions=
</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Vault is deployed in a containerized environment using Docker Compose</p=
></li>
<li>
<p>Vault is initialized using Shamir Secret Sharing, with unseal keys distr=
ibuted manually</p></li>
<li>
<p>Environment variables (e.g., <code>VAULT_DEV_ROOT_TOKEN_ID</code>) are s=
et via <code>.env</code> files or securely passed into containers</p></li>
<li>
<p>Persistent storage is mounted from the host filesystem</p></li>
<li>
<p>Vault uses Consul as a storage backend</p></li>
<li>
<p>TLS is enabled for all communication</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-ConfigurationOverview">Configu=
ration Overview</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Storage backend</strong>: Consul</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Listener</strong>: TCP with TLS enabled</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Vault UI</strong>: Enabled</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Initialization</strong>: Manual (<code>vault operator init</code=
>)</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Unsealing</strong>: Manual (<code>vault operator unseal</code>),=
 using Shamir Secret Sharing (e.g., 5 key shares, 3 threshold)</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Root token handling</strong>: Manual (secure distribution offlin=
e)</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Configuration</strong>: Provided via the <code>VAULT_LOCAL_CONFI=
G</code> environment variable</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-StandaloneDeployment">Standalo=
ne Deployment</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-VaultConfiguration(Standalone)=
">Vault Configuration (Standalone)</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">storage=
 "consul" {
  address      =3D "https://consul:8500"  # Consul address, include port
  path         =3D "vault/"               # Path in Consul KV
  tls_ca_file  =3D "/vault/certs/ca.crt"
  tls_cert_file =3D "/vault/certs/vault.crt"
  tls_key_file  =3D "/vault/certs/vault.key"
}

listener "tcp" {
  address        =3D "0.0.0.0:8200"
  tls_cert_file  =3D "/vault/certs/vault.crt"
  tls_key_file   =3D "/vault/certs/vault.key"
  client_cert_auth =3D "require"  # Require client certificates
}

ui =3D true
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>tls_ca_file</strong>: Path to the CA certificate</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>tls_cert_file</strong>: Path to the Vault server certificate</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>tls_key_file</strong>: Path to the Vault server private key</p><=
/li>
<li>
<p><strong>client_cert_auth</strong>: Set to "require" to enable mTLS</p></=
li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-Initialization&amp;UnsealProce=
ss(Standalone)">Initialization &amp; Unseal Process (Standalone)</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Start Consul</p></li>
<li>
<p>Start Vault</p></li>
<li>
<p>Execute a shell within the Vault container:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">docker =
exec -it vault sh
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Initialize Vault:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">vault o=
perator init -key-shares=3D5 -key-threshold=3D3
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Securely store the output, which includes:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>5 unseal keys</p></li>
<li>
<p>1 root token</p></li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Important</strong>: These keys are non-recoverable. DO NOT LOSE =
THEM!</p></li>
<li>
<p>Unseal Vault with any 3 of the 5 unseal keys:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">vault o=
perator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://0.0.0.0:8200 &lt;key1&gt;
vault operator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://0.0.0.0:8200 &lt;key2&gt;
vault operator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://0.0.0.0:8200 &lt;key3&gt;
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Vault becomes available after unsealing</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-ClusteredDeployment">Clustered=
 Deployment</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-VaultConfiguration(Clustered)"=
>Vault Configuration (Clustered)</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">storage=
 "consul" {
  address      =3D "https://consul1:8500,https://consul2:8500,https://consu=
l3:8500"  # Comma-separated list of Consul addresses
  path         =3D "vault/"
  tls_ca_file  =3D "/vault/certs/ca.crt"
  tls_cert_file =3D "/vault/certs/vault.crt"
  tls_key_file  =3D "/vault/certs/vault.key"
}

listener "tcp" {
  address        =3D "0.0.0.0:8200"
  tls_cert_file  =3D "/vault/certs/vault.crt"
  tls_key_file   =3D "/vault/certs/vault.key"
  client_cert_auth =3D "require"
}

cluster_name =3D "vault-cluster"
ui =3D true
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>address</strong>: Comma-separated list of Consul servers</p></li=
>
<li>
<p><strong>cluster_name</strong>: The name of the Vault cluster</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-InitializationandUnsealProcess=
(Clustered)">Initialization and Unseal Process (Clustered)</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Start Consul cluster (3 or 5 servers)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Start Vault instances (at least 3 for HA)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Initialize only one Vault instance:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">docker =
exec -it vault-node-1 sh
vault operator init -key-shares=3D5 -key-threshold=3D3
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Securely store the unseal keys and root token</p></li>
<li>
<p>Unseal the same Vault instance that was initialized:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">vault o=
perator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-1:8200 &lt;key1&gt;
vault operator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-1:8200 &lt;key2&gt=
;
vault operator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-1:8200 &lt;key3&gt=
;
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Join the other Vault instances to the cluster after the first node is un=
sealed:</p>
<p>On vault-node-2:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">vault o=
perator join -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-1:8200 -tls
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>On vault-node-3:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">vault o=
perator join -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-1:8200 -tls
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Unseal the other Vault instances, one at a time, using keys from the ini=
tial unseal process:</p>
<p>On vault-node-2:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">vault o=
perator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-2:8200 &lt;key1&gt;
vault operator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-2:8200 &lt;key2&gt=
;
vault operator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-2:8200 &lt;key3&gt=
;
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>On vault-node-3:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">vault o=
perator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-3:8200 &lt;key1&gt;
vault operator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-3:8200 &lt;key2&gt=
;
vault operator unseal -tls -address=3Dhttps://vault-node-3:8200 &lt;key3&gt=
;
</pre>
</div>
</div></li>
<li>
<p>Vault cluster is available after all nodes are unsealed</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-ConsulSetup">Consul Setup</h2>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-Pre-Conditions.1">Pre-Conditio=
ns</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Consul is deployed using Docker Compose</p></li>
<li>
<p>TLS is enabled for all communication</p></li>
<li>
<p>Consul is used to provide distributed configuration and store Vault data=
</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-ConfigurationOverview.1">Confi=
guration Overview</h3>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Mode</strong>: Server (standalone or clustered)</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>DNS</strong>: Disabled</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Client mode</strong>: Disabled</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>UI</strong>: Enabled</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Storage</strong>: Local disk</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>TLS</strong>: Enabled</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-ConsulConfiguration(Standalone=
)">Consul Configuration (Standalone)</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">server =
=3D true
bootstrap_expect =3D 1
ui =3D true
client_addr =3D "0.0.0.0"
bind_addr =3D "0.0.0.0"
datacenter =3D "dc1"

tls {
  enabled =3D true
  cert_file =3D "/consul/certs/consul.crt"
  key_file  =3D "/consul/certs/consul.key"
  ca_file   =3D "/consul/certs/ca.crt"
  verify_incoming =3D true
  verify_outgoing =3D true
}
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-ConsulConfiguration(Clustered)=
">Consul Configuration (Clustered)</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">server =
=3D true
bootstrap_expect =3D 3  # or 5
ui =3D true
client_addr =3D "0.0.0.0"
bind_addr =3D "0.0.0.0"
datacenter =3D "dc1"

tls {
  enabled =3D true
  cert_file =3D "/consul/certs/consul.crt"
  key_file  =3D "/consul/certs/consul.key"
  ca_file   =3D "/consul/certs/ca.crt"
  verify_incoming =3D true
  verify_outgoing =3D true
}

retry_join =3D ["consul1", "consul2", "consul3"]  # For each server
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>retry_join</strong>: Used to join the other Consul servers. Use =
the private IPs or container names of the other Consul nodes.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-DockerComposeSetup">Docker Com=
pose Setup</h2>
<p>A basic <code>docker-compose.yml</code> file orchestrates the Vault and =
Consul services. All volumes are mapped locally, and networking is confined=
 to a dedicated Docker network.</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">version=
: '3.8'
services:
  consul:
    image: hashicorp/consul:1.15
    container_name: consul
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "8500:8500"
      - "8600:8600/udp"
    command: agent -server -bootstrap-expect=3D1 -ui -client=3D0.0.0.0 -bin=
d=3D0.0.0.0 -data-dir=3D/consul/data -hcl=3D'tls { enabled =3D true; cert_f=
ile =3D "/consul/certs/consul.crt"; key_file =3D "/consul/certs/consul.key"=
; ca_file =3D "/consul/certs/ca.crt"; verify_incoming =3D true; verify_outg=
oing =3D true }'
    volumes:
      - ./consul/data:/consul/data
      - ./certs:/consul/certs  # Mount certs
    networks:
      - vault-consul  # Define a network

  consul2:  # For Consul Cluster
    image: hashicorp/consul:1.15
    container_name: consul2
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "8502:8500"
      - "8602:8600/udp"
    command: agent -server -retry-join=3D"consul:8500" -ui -client=3D0.0.0.=
0 -bind=3D0.0.0.0 -data-dir=3D/consul/data -hcl=3D'tls { enabled =3D true; =
cert_file =3D "/consul/certs/consul.crt"; key_file =3D "/consul/certs/consu=
l.key"; ca_file =3D "/consul/certs/ca.crt"; verify_incoming =3D true; verif=
y_outgoing =3D true }'
    volumes:
      - ./consul/data2:/consul/data
      - ./certs:/consul/certs
    networks:
      - vault-consul

  consul3:  # For Consul Cluster
    image: hashicorp/consul:1.15
    container_name: consul3
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "8503:8500"
      - "8603:8600/udp"
    command: agent -server -retry-join=3D"consul:8500" -retry-join=3D"consu=
l2:8502" -ui -client=3D0.0.0.0 -bind=3D0.0.0.0 -data-dir=3D/consul/data -hc=
l=3D'tls { enabled =3D true; cert_file =3D "/consul/certs/consul.crt"; key_=
file =3D "/consul/certs/consul.key"; ca_file =3D "/consul/certs/ca.crt"; ve=
rify_incoming =3D true; verify_outgoing =3D true }'
    volumes:
      - ./consul/data3:/consul/data
      - ./certs:/consul/certs
    networks:
      - vault-consul

  vault:
    image: hashicorp/vault:1.15
    container_name: vault
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "8200:8200"
    cap_add:
      - IPC_LOCK
    environment:
      VAULT_ADDR: https://0.0.0.0:8200  # Use https
      VAULT_API_ADDR: https://localhost:8200  # Use https
      VAULT_LOCAL_CONFIG: |
        storage "consul" {
          address =3D "https://consul:8500"  # Use https
          path    =3D "vault/"
          tls_ca_file   =3D "/vault/certs/ca.crt"
          tls_cert_file =3D "/vault/certs/vault.crt"
          tls_key_file  =3D "/vault/certs/vault.key"
        }
        listener "tcp" {
          address     =3D "0.0.0.0:8200"
          tls_cert_file =3D "/vault/certs/vault.crt"
          tls_key_file  =3D "/vault/certs/vault.key"
          client_cert_auth =3D "require"  # Require client certs
        }
        ui =3D true
    volumes:
      - ./vault/data:/vault/file
      - ./certs:/vault/certs  # Mount certs
    depends_on:
      - consul
    networks:
      - vault-consul

networks:
  vault-consul:  # Define network
</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p>Key features of the Docker Compose file:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>A network <code>vault-consul</code> is defined and used by both Vault an=
d Consul</p></li>
<li>
<p>Consul ports are mapped individually for each Consul server in the clust=
er (8500, 8502, 8503)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Consul TLS settings are included in the command using <code>-hcl</code><=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>Certificates are mounted into both Consul and Vault containers</p></li>
<li>
<p>Vault addresses are updated to use https</p></li>
<li>
<p>Consul service definitions are added</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"AI-354-AI+ConfigurationandSecurity-KubernetesIntegration">Kuberne=
tes Integration</h2>
<p>When moving to Kubernetes, consider the following changes:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Helm Charts</strong>: Use the official Vault and Consul Helm cha=
rts</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Auto-Unseal</strong>: Configure auto-unseal with cloud provider =
KMS</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Secret Injection</strong>: Use Vault's Kubernetes auth method fo=
r injecting secrets</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Service Mesh</strong>: Evaluate Consul Connect for service mesh =
capabilities</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Storage</strong>: Consider using Consul or integrated storage fo=
r Vault</p></li>
</ol>
<p>Example Vault Helm values for Kubernetes:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: bash; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">server:
  ha:
    enabled: true
    replicas: 3
 =20
  extraEnvironmentVars:
    VAULT_CACERT: /vault/certs/ca.crt
    VAULT_TLSCERT: /vault/certs/vault.crt
    VAULT_TLSKEY: /vault/certs/vault.key
 =20
  volumes:
    - name: certs
      secret:
        secretName: vault-certs
 =20
  volumeMounts:
    - name: certs
      mountPath: /vault/certs
      readOnly: true
</pre>
</div>
</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
